  "notes": {
    "raw": "Phase change: 1016 K, incongruent melting point of $FeS_{2}$ ; decomposition pressure equals approximately 10 atm. \nHeat capacity (cal/mol·K) and enthalpy (kcal/mol) equations: \n$$\n\\begin{array}{r l} 2 9 8. 1 5 - 1 0 0 0 \\mathrm{K}: & \\mathrm{Cp} ^ {\\circ} = 1 6. 4 6 1 + 3. 3 4 6 \\times 1 0 ^ {- 3} \\mathrm{T} - 2. 3 2 0 \\times 1 0 ^ {5} \\mathrm{T} ^ {- 2} \\\\ & \\mathrm{H} ^ {\\circ} - \\mathrm{H} _ {2 9 8} ^ {\\circ} = 1 6. 4 6 1 \\times 1 0 ^ {- 3} \\mathrm{T} + 1. 6 7 3 \\times 1 0 ^ {- 6} \\mathrm{T} ^ {2} + 2. 3 2 0 \\times 1 0 ^ {2} \\mathrm{T} ^ {- 1} - 5. 8 3 5 \\end{array}\n$$\nReaction equations (kcal/mol): \n$$\n\\begin{array}{l} 2 9 8. 1 5 - 1 0 0 0 \\mathrm{K}: \\quad \\Delta \\mathrm{Hr} ^ {\\circ} = - 7 5. 0 9 2 + 8. 3 3 9 \\times 1 0 ^ {- 3} \\mathrm{T} - 4. 7 1 8 \\times 1 0 ^ {- 6} \\mathrm{T} ^ {2} + 3 9 2. 2 0 0 \\mathrm{T} ^ {- 1} \\\\ \\Delta \\mathrm{Gr} ^ {\\circ} = - 7 5. 0 9 2 - 8. 3 3 9 \\times 1 0 ^ {- 3} \\mathrm{T} \\ln \\mathrm{T} + 4. 7 1 8 \\times 1 0 ^ {- 6} \\mathrm{T} ^ {2} + 1 9 6. 1 0 0 \\mathrm{T} ^ {- 1} + 1 0 3. 6 2 3 \\times 1 0 ^ {- 3} \\mathrm{T} \\end{array}\n$$\nSource: Data from Chase (17). ",
